**Given:**

Principal (P) = ₹3000

Rate of Interest (R) = 8% per annum

Time (T) = 3 years

**Formula used:**

Simple Interest (SI) = dfrac{P times R times T}{100}

**Calculations:**

SI = dfrac{3000 times 8 times 3}{100}

⇒ SI = dfrac{3000 times 24}{100}

⇒ SI = dfrac{72000}{100}

⇒ SI = ₹720

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**

**Given:**

Refractive index values: 1.32, 1.37, 1.36, 1.39, 1.31

**Formula used:**

Average = dfrac{{Sum of observations}}{{Number of observations}}

**Calculation:**

Average = dfrac{1.32 + 1.37 + 1.36 + 1.39 + 1.31}{5}

⇒ Average = dfrac{6.75}{5}

⇒ Average = 1.35

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**
